asus-zenbook-linux-tools (1.0.9) resolute; urgency=medium

  * SonarQube Cloud cleanup of the shell code base (behaviour-preserving):
    [[ ]] tests, explicit returns, default case arms, named locals, hoisted
    constants, helper extractions (CCN <= 5) and file splits (<= 600 lines).
  * Esc on the Display Toggle OSD dismisses it without applying the layout:
    one ordered ydotool/xdotool injection (no --clearmodifiers), stale .cancel
    markers expire after 3s, and the daemon's cancel timeout defaults to 1.0s.
  * asus-sound-fix.sh and asus-screenpad-brightness.sh avoid $((10#x)) so
    SonarQube can parse them.
  * Zero-padded numbers (08, 0150) are read as decimal again in the install
    command timeout clamps, the test-mode root check and the fan profile value.
  * Esc/Cancel in the installer component checklist aborts the install instead
    of falling back to the text prompt.
  * tests/e2e/real is a package again so run_real_e2e.sh discovers its tests;
    kcov coverage kept at >= 90% for asus-common and install-mate.
  * Pattern checks use grep here-strings instead of printf|grep -q, which
    could SIGPIPE under pipefail and intermittently fail container uninstalls.
  * Hardware-validated on the ZenBook Pro Duo UX582HS (Ubuntu 26.04, GNOME).

 -- ventura8 <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:38:37 +0300

asus-zenbook-linux-tools (1.0.8) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Hardened bin/asus_hda_verb.py: the hwdep device path from the command line
    is now confined to /dev/snd (DEV_SND_ROOT for test fixtures) and must name
    an hwC<N>D<M> node, so the root helper cannot be pointed at another file.
  * CI/security hygiene: pinned and wheels-only coverage install, npm installs
    with --ignore-scripts, curl restricted to HTTPS (--proto '=https'), and the
    loginctl test stub written owner-only.
  * SonarQube Cloud project renamed to asus-zenbook-linux-tools.
  * pylint 4.0.9.

